## Claim
Text: "The Iowa Farm Bureau, US says that it would no longer be endorsing US Republican Iowa Sen. Joni Ernst for her re-election"
Claim date: October 18, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Is the Iowa Farm Bureau an actual agricultural organization based in Iowa?
Answer: Yes, the Iowa Farm Bureau is an actual agricultural organization based in Iowa. The source states it "was created to advocate for Iowa’s farmers and rural communities" and "sets the conversation on agricultural policy" in the state.

Source URL: https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/opinion/columnists/iowa-view/2018/06/22/iowa-farm-bureau-insurance-company-voice-farmers/714274002/

### Is Joni Ernst the incumbent Republican U.S. Senator from Iowa as of 2020?
Answer: Yes, Joni Ernst was the incumbent Republican U.S. Senator from Iowa in 2020, as evidenced by her official Senate website stating she was "now representing Iowans in the United States Senate."

Source URL: https://www.ernst.senate.gov/about

### Did the Iowa Farm Bureau officially endorse Joni Ernst in a prior election cycle before 2020?
Answer: Yes, the Iowa Farm Bureau did officially endorse Joni Ernst in a prior election cycle, as indicated by the statement that "the Iowa Farm Bureau was proud to designate her as a Friend of Agriculture."

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/Statement-by-Iowa-Farm-Bureau-Federation

### On or around October 18, 2020, did the Iowa Farm Bureau issue a public statement regarding its endorsements for the 2020 general election?
Answer: Yes, the Iowa Farm Bureau did issue a public statement regarding its 2020 general election endorsements. Specifically, its Political Action Committee (PAC) publicly designated Senator Joni Ernst as a "Friend of Agriculture," with the statement noting that details on all designees could be found in the "September 9 or October 21 Iowa Farm Bureau Spokesman newspaper."

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag

### Does the Iowa Farm Bureau's official communication for the 2020 election cycle state that it is not endorsing Senator Joni Ernst for re-election?
Answer: No, the Iowa Farm Bureau's official communication for the 2020 election cycle does not state that it is not endorsing Senator Joni Ernst; in fact, it states the opposite. The search result cites the Farm Bureau's political arm endorsing Ernst, with a news release quoting the chairman of the Farm Bureau PAC: "Candidates earn the Friend of Agriculture designation (endorsement) by supporting issues that directly impact Iowa’s agricultural economy."

Source URL: https://qctimes.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/campaign-almanac-for-wednesday-september-9-2020/article_78f6dbc5-6272-547c-9de9-e2a78cefb8cf.html

### Does the Iowa Farm Bureau's communication explicitly characterize this as withdrawing or ending a previous endorsement, as opposed to simply not issuing a new one?
Answer: The search result does not contain information about withdrawing or ending a previous endorsement; instead, it announces that the Iowa Farm Bureau PAC designated Senator Joni Ernst as a "Friend of Agriculture" for the 2020 general election.

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag

### What is the stated reason provided by the Iowa Farm Bureau for not endorsing Senator Joni Ernst?
Answer: The Iowa Farm Bureau did not state a reason for not endorsing Senator Joni Ernst because, according to their official announcement, they actually designated her as a "Friend of Agriculture" for the 2020 election, citing her support for their policies and voting record.

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag

### Has the Iowa Farm Bureau endorsed other Republican candidates in Iowa for the 2020 election, as per the same official communication?
Answer: Yes, the Iowa Farm Bureau endorsed another Republican candidate, Randy Feenstra, for Iowa's 4th Congressional District race in the 2020 election, as per the same official communication. The source states: "The Iowa Farm Bureau’s political arm endorsed Republicans Joni Ernst and Randy Feenstra in their respective election races."

Source URL: https://qctimes.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/campaign-almanac-for-wednesday-september-9-2020/article_78f6dbc5-6272-547c-9de9-e2a78cefb8cf.html

### Has Senator Joni Ernst's campaign issued a public response to the Iowa Farm Bureau's decision not to endorse her?
Answer: The search result indicates that the Iowa Farm Bureau has publicly stated that the claim about withdrawing endorsement is based on a fake email, and they reaffirm their support for Senator Ernst, making a response from her campaign to a non-existent decision unnecessary.

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/Statement-by-Iowa-Farm-Bureau-Federation

### Is there any official record, such as a press release archived on their website or reported by a reputable news outlet, that documents the Iowa Farm Bureau's announcement from October 2020?
Answer: The search result contains an official Iowa Farm Bureau article from October 21, 2020, which documents the opposite of the claim: the Iowa Farm Bureau Political Action Committee officially designated Senator Joni Ernst as a "Friend of Agriculture" for the 2020 general election.

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag

## Final Judgement
Based on the fact-check, all retrieved official communications from the Iowa Farm Bureau around the October 18, 2020, claim date consistently show the organization reaffirming its support for Senator Joni Ernst. Specifically, the Iowa Farm Bureau's Political Action Committee (PAC) officially designated her as a "Friend of Agriculture" on September 9, 2020, a fact repeated in their October 21, 2020 publication. A separate statement from the Bureau also explicitly calls a rumor of a withdrawn endorsement a "fake email." No evidence was found showing any withdrawal, retraction, or non-endorsement.

The evidence is clear and directly from official sources, leaving no ambiguity or missing information to investigate further. The claim that the Iowa Farm Bureau said it would no longer endorse Joni Ernst is explicitly and factually contradicted by the organization's own public statements from the relevant period.

`refuted`

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The Iowa Farm Bureau officially affirmed its endorsement of Senator Joni Ernst for the 2020 election, as its Political Action Committee designated her a "Friend of Agriculture" on [September 9, 2020](https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag) and again in an [October 21, 2020](https://qctimes.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/campaign-almanac-for-wednesday-september-9-2020/article_78f6dbc5-6272-547c-9de9-e2a78cefb8cf.html) publication. The organization explicitly identified the claim of a withdrawn endorsement as a "fake email" in a [public statement](https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/Statement-by-Iowa-Farm-Bureau-Federation), finding no evidence of any retraction or non-endorsement.